mode.description:
How to handle a save that targets an existing memory (same title or conversationId). "replace" (default) overwrites the existing content with what you send. "append" concatenates new content below the existing content with a timestamped separator (

--- UPDATE <ISO8601> ---

). Use "append" for living documents you genuinely want to grow over time; use "replace" for one-shot snapshots and ad-hoc captures. The /save skill defaults to "append" automatically — you only need to pass this for explicit overrides.
